"""Tile the windows of the current workspace into columns, rows or a grid.

  flashback-tile auto|4|3|2|rows-3|rows-2|grid-2x2|grid-3x2|grid-4x2|restore
                      auto uses the counts for the screen size (see the
                      settings), 4, 3 and 2 are columns, rows-3 and rows-2
                      rows, grid-CxR a grid; restore puts the windows back
                      where they were before tiling
  flashback-tile N | rows N | CxR
                      N columns, N rows, or C columns and R rows
  flashback-tile toggle snap|tile-new|disabled|vertical|horizontal
                      flip a switch: automatic tiling (snapping dropped
                      windows), tiling new windows, all tiling, or tiling
                      into columns or rows (one of those two stays on)
  flashback-tile get-toggles
                      print the switches, as KEY=true|false
  flashback-tile menu rebuild this user's Window Tiling panel menu from the
                      settings and the keyboard shortcuts
  flashback-tile default-shortcuts
                      give the tiling actions their default keys, once per
                      user (used at login)
  flashback-tile export FILE
                      save the settings of the tiling and resolution menus
                      and the keyboard shortcuts to FILE
  flashback-tile import FILE
                      load them from FILE
  flashback-tile snap-daemon
                      while automatic tiling, tiling new windows or
                      resizing neighbouring windows together is on,
                      snap each window dropped with the mouse into the
                      column, row or grid cell under the pointer, and tile
                      each new window with the others on its screen
"""
